      "imagePrompt": "An annual salary being divided into several paychecks across a calendar."
    },
    {
      "title": "Taxes come out",
      "text": "Employers generally withhold money from each paycheck for federal and state income taxes, plus Social Security and Medicare. These payments go to the government instead of into your bank account.",
      "imagePrompt": "A paycheck being split into a bank deposit and labeled portions for federal tax, state tax, Social Security, and Medicare."
    },
    {
      "title": "Benefits can add up",
      "text": "Your paycheck may also pay for benefits you chose, such as health insurance or a 401(k) contribution. Some deductions come out before taxes are calculated; others come out after.",
      "imagePrompt": "A paycheck with portions going toward health insurance and a 401(k), alongside the remaining take-home pay."
